    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "A dataset is normally distributed with a mean of 75 and a standard deviation of 12. By first calculating the standardised score and using the standard normal distribution table below, find the probability that a randomly chosen score satisfies each condition.\n\nRound z-scores to 2 decimal places where necessary and give probabilities to 4 decimal places. Here $Z$ has the standard normal distribution.\n\n| $z$ | $P(Z\\le z)$ |\n|---|---|\n| 0.08 | 0.5319 |\n| 0.33 | 0.6293 |\n| 0.42 | 0.6628 |\n| 0.75 | 0.7734 |\n| 1.00 | 0.8413 |\n| 1.25 | 0.8943 |\n| 2.08 | 0.9812 |\n| 2.58 | 0.9951 |",
